ed to prevent SQL Injection.\n4. **CSRF Protection**: Implement CSRF tokens in all forms and validate them on the server side.\n5. **Secure Cookies**: Set the `Secure`, `HttpOnly`, and `SameSite` attributes for cookies.\n\n### Consultation with OWASP:\nFor further details on these vulnerabilities and their mitigations, refer to the OWASP Top Ten and other security standards.\n\nIf you need more detailed information on any specific vulnerability, please let me know!', 'findings_count': 739}
